Overview

Upgraded a friend’s existing PC with a focus on improving gaming performance, 
maintaining compatibility, and reducing total upgrade cost by reusing reliable existing hardware where possible.

Component Upgrades

Processor       Intel CPU | AMD CPU
Motherboard     AM4 Intel | AM4 AMD
Memory          Existing 64GB DDR4
Graphics Card   RTX 3060  | Radeon RX 9070 XT
Power Supply    600W PSU  | 850W PSU
Storage         Existing Storage Reused
Case            Existing Case Reused

Process

Evaluated the current system hardware, performance limitations, and budget goals. 
Planned an upgrade path that retained the AM4 motherboard and existing 64GB DDR4 memory to avoid unnecessary replacement costs. 
Installed the new CPU, graphics card, and upgraded power supply. 
Verified hardware compatibility, updated drivers, and tested system stability after installation.

Skills Learned

Cost-effective upgrade planning
Hardware compatibility analysis
Platform lifecycle management
Power supply sizing
Component installation
Driver updates and maintenance
Performance optimization
System stability testing
